Emerging Market Opportunities
Growing Adoption of Non-Contact Profilometry
Non-contact optical and laser-based technologies offer opportunities for inspecting sensitive wafer surfaces without physical interaction. Their relevance is increasing in applications involving advanced materials, MEMS, and complex semiconductor structures.

AI-Enabled Measurement and Predictive Analytics
Artificial intelligence and machine learning can enhance defect identification, measurement analysis, and process monitoring. Integration with predictive analytics may help manufacturers detect process deviations earlier and improve production consistency.

Expanding Compound Semiconductor Applications
Growing applications for silicon carbide and gallium nitride in power electronics and RF devices are creating demand for specialized wafer characterization. Profiling systems capable of handling different substrate materials and surface structures could benefit from this development.

